    "narrative": "The offensive engine for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on the high-upside pairing of **Corbin Carroll** and **James Wood** today. **Corbin Carroll** leads the squad with an 85.84 rating, buoyed by a favorable matchup against Ure\u00f1a and the high-leverage production spot in the three-hole. Meanwhile, **James Wood** (76.28) is a mandatory start; his elite 0.403 xwOBA combined with a prime leadoff opportunity against the vulnerable Spence makes him our most efficient generator of Runs and SB. **Gabriel Moreno** and **Seiya Suzuki** also provide sturdy middle-of-the-order production, with **Seiya Suzuki** receiving a slight boost from favorable wind conditions that amplify his power potential against Lorenzen.\n\nThe tightest roster construction decision involved **Kyle Karros**, whose 49.66 score narrowly kept him in the UTIL slot over alternative configurations. While the platoon advantage against Imanaga provides a marginal lift, the matchup against a high-tier arm creates significant volatility. We are closely monitoring **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**, both of whom are facing Nick Martinez; their sub-60 efficiency scores reflect the difficulty of the matchup, but their presence remains necessary to capture potential counting stats in the lower half of the order. While we are currently managing the absences of **Mickey Moniak** and **Trevor Story** on the IL, alongside the off-day for **Jose Caballero** and **Josh Naylor**, our depth remains focused on maintaining category integrity, particularly in the stolen base department. Investors should remain cautious of the volatility inherent in the **Zach McKinstry** start, as his 43.13 rating places him right on the edge of our viability floor; should his spot in the order drop further or defensive substitutions accelerate, he is the primary candidate for an early hook to preserve our cap.",
